Subject: [PATCH 4/7] i686: model the unsuffixed xchg in the peephole register
 oracle

line_reg_use_def special-cases xchg so that both operands count as read AND
written: the central implicit-operand oracle knows a single destination, and the
comment above the code already warns that a missing half can make CFG DCE delete
a live dividend or string pointer. The match was on "xchgl" | "xchgw" | "xchgb"
- but GAS accepts the bare mnemonic and infers the width from the registers, so
`xchg %esp, %ebx` measured uses=0x18, defs=0x000. A plain read, as far as every
guard built on this oracle is concerned: dead-register proofs, copy propagation,
and the slot windows of the x87 staging fold.

It is reachable only through inline asm or hand-written .s (the emitter always
suffixes), which is exactly why it survived 25 CI gates, 2,497 unit tests, a
250-program differential fuzz and a 792-TU corpus A/B: a corpus cannot find
defects the corpus does not contain. Measurement finds regressions; only
adversarial construction finds blind spots, which is why this is pinned by tests
rather than left as a note.

The x87 fold itself was already safe without this fix, for a principled reason
worth recording: function_forms_frame_addr runs a taint fixpoint seeded at %esp
over operand TEXT, mnemonic-agnostically, so the xchg taints %ebx and condition
(4) refuses the whole function. Two tests now pin that behaviour
(x87_gp_pair_staging_not_folded_when_esp_is_exchanged_in_the_window and
..._after_the_load), so the guard cannot silently become accidental.

Fix the oracle anyway, because other passes consume it: match the mnemonic
prefix and mark every referenced register as both read and written, for the
bare, 32-bit and byte forms. Measured effect on the 792-TU corpus:
byte-identical - with the fold disabled the corpus still totals exactly 271,585
instructions / 102,701 frame-slot references, the recorded pre-fold baseline -
so this adds soundness without changing one emitted instruction.
