From febfca04bb6f9fa35ed0001c818fe6f9aee1d187 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <t@t>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 12:43:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] i686: fold the store-side mirror of x87 GP-pair staging

The load side removes the GP-pair round-trip on the way INTO the x87 unit. This
removes it on the way OUT, where the backend pops a double into a frame slot,
reads it straight back through a GP pair, and writes it to its real destination
four bytes at a time:

    fstpl S                  fstpl M
    movl S,   %r1       ->
    movl S+4, %r2
    movl %r1, M
    movl %r2, M+4

`fstpl` already stores all eight bytes in exactly the little-endian layout the
two `movl`s produce, so the rewrite retargets the x87 store and deletes the four
GP lines. The mnemonic is kept verbatim, which preserves the x87 pop and lets the
non-popping `fstl` ride the same path with no extra argument -- a test pins that,
because silently turning `fstl` into `fstpl` would drop an x87 register.

Eight conditions: the load side's six, plus two that only exist here. `M` must
not be able to name the slot bytes (a `%ebp` component is refused; an `%esp`
destination is accepted only when the two 8-byte ranges are disjoint -- partial
overlap is the miscompile, since with `M = S+2` the original leaves the pair's
bytes at `S+2..S+10` while `fstpl S+2` writes the same double in a different
layout), and no register in `M`'s addressing expression may be `%r1`/`%r2`,
because the write to `M` moves AHEAD of the loads that define them.

Measured on the 792-TU i686 corpus with two independent kill switches, so each
half is attributable: both off 271,585 instructions / 102,701 slot refs; load
side only 270,637 / 101,990, reproducing the previously recorded numbers exactly,
which is the proof that the two passes do not interfere; both on 270,349 /
101,774. The store side is -288 instructions (-0.1064%), -216 slot refs, 15 TUs
changed, none worse; combined -1,236 (-0.4551%). Per TU (base -> load -> both):
fp_domain_crossing 1077 -> 961 -> 861, nbody 1485 -> 1357 -> 1349,
vectorize_matmul_n16 2611 -> 2483 -> 2475.

Refusal profile, measured by re-implementing the cheap textual conditions over
the baseline arm's 247 strict candidates: 31 refused by the `%ebp` rule, 0 by
slot overlap, 0 by the pair addressing its own destination, 0 by the frame-address
taint, and 216 reaching the whole-function conditions -- of which 72 fold and 144
are refused by the dead-store post-condition or register liveness. That
post-condition gives up at Call/InlineAsm/JmpIndirect; relaxing it looks sound
under the frame-address condition (no register holds a frame address, so no
argument can point into the frame, and a callee's own frame is below %esp) but it
needs an adversary for the route the taint fixpoint cannot see, so it is filed in
the FOLLOWUP rather than done here.

Runtime is NOT claimed: nbody 0.925 combined against 0.920/0.925 for the load
side alone, matmul 0.988, vector_remainder 1.013 -- all inside the noise floor.
This lands as a 0-regression completion of the transformation family, not as a
performance win, and the docs say so in those words.

Correctness: 11 new unit tests -- five positive (basic, SIB destination, disjoint
frame destination, the non-popping `fstl` form, across a loop back edge) and six
negative each carrying its own positive control (overlapping destination,
destination addressed by the pair, `%ebp` destination, slot read again, pair still
live, sequence not adjacent). cargo test --lib: 2,508 passed, 0 failed.
Byte-identity scan: 40 TUs changed corpus-wide. Execution differential over those
40: 0 assembly failures, 0 off-vs-on differences, 35 ran and matched, 31
byte-identical to gcc -m32 -O2, the same 4 pre-existing divergences.
ci_local.sh --fast: 25 passed, 0 failed, 3 skipped; clippy -D warnings clean.

The differential fuzz exposed a hole in the harness rather than in the pass: the
first 340-program run after this change reported exactly the pre-change census,
because none of the 11 generators can produce the store-side shape. Six were
added (three that produce it, three adversaries: destination address taken,
volatile destination, a call between the store and the slot's retirement); the
re-run gives 340/340 built and ran, 134 fired, g_store_indexed_stride 20/20 and
g_store_struct_out 20/20, every store adversary 0/20, 0 hard failures.
